        "status": "success",
        "rationale": "The requirement has one behavioral obligation. When a prepared tool result is sent again, either during a provider retry or on a later conversation turn, the tool's `calls` and `result_bytes` must stay unchanged.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[tool_usage_counts_utf8_results_and_errors_once_across_retries]` covers both cases:\n- **Retry:** The first provider turn returns three tool calls: two `read_node` and one `lookup`. The `Scenario` provider then returns a throttled error for the next request. That request carries the prepared results, so the retry sends them again. The final turn is another successful tool-call turn, which also sends the earlier results again as history.\n- **Later turn:** The final assertion requires `read_node` to be exactly `{calls:2, result_bytes:1280}`, `lookup` to be `{1, 6}` and `submit_result` to be `{1, 0}`. If a re-send had been counted again, these totals would be larger.\n\n`generic_conversations_can_use_default_telemetry_through_retry_and_continuation` adds a second scenario with a retry, a `FinishReason::Length` continuation and a later turn. It asserts `lookup.calls == 1`, that `lookup.result_bytes` equals the `\"fixture answer\"` length, and that `submit_result` stays at 1 call and 0 bytes. It also asserts that `session.dispatched == 1`. The final request history contains the earlier result, so the prepared result was sent again without changing the counts.\n\nBoth tests carry `{test}` references to `ToolUsage.replay`, and I found no gap."
      }
